<pre class=metadata>
Title: Foo
Group: test
Shortname: foo
Level: 1
Status: LS
ED: http://example.com/foo
Abstract: Testing linking of the getter/setter/deleter keywords of unnamed special operations to their method dfns. FooDefined defines them, FooUndefined does not and must not produce errors. FooNamed has a named getter, whose keyword stays unlinked.
Editor: Example Editor
Date: 1970-01-01
</pre>

<xmp class=idl>
[Exposed=Window]
interface FooDefined {
	getter DOMString (unsigned long index);
	setter undefined (unsigned long index, DOMString value);
	deleter undefined (DOMString name);
};

[Exposed=Window]
interface FooUndefined {
	getter DOMString (unsigned long index);
	setter undefined (unsigned long index, DOMString value);
};

[Exposed=Window]
interface FooNamed {
	getter DOMString item(unsigned long index);
};
</xmp>

The <dfn method for=FooDefined lt="__getter__(index)">indexed property getter</dfn> returns the item at |index|.

The <dfn method for=FooDefined lt="__setter__(index, value)">indexed property setter</dfn> replaces the item at |index|.

The <dfn method for=FooDefined lt="__deleter__(name)">named property deleter</dfn> removes the named item.

The <dfn method for=FooNamed>item(index)</dfn> method returns the item at |index|.
